[1m[38;5;231mWhat should the userId parameter actually carry?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m Client correlation ID (Recommended)
     [38;5;246mCaller mints a per-attempt ID and passes it to login(). Works with data available at call time; traces failed [39m
     [38;5;246mattempts too.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Caller-supplied account ID
     [38;5;246mlogin(userId, username, password). Requires a new source for the real account ID — form field or pre-login lookup.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Return it instead
     [38;5;246mKeep the signature; add userId to login()'s return value, as a server would assign it. Not a parameter.[39m
